data
  root
    label 8 pooling failure modes
    children
      - label Hold-time failures (a-d)
        children
          - label a) Pool exhaustion from slow queries
          - label b) Idle-in-transaction draining the pool
          - label c) External API call inside a transaction
          - label d) NAT/firewall silently drops idle TCP
      - label State-management failures (e-f)
        children
          - label e) Prepared-statement collisions (pre-1.21)
          - label f) State leak between clients (no DISCARD ALL)
      - label Capacity failures (g-h)
        children
          - label g) Pool sized for steady-state, not spikes
          - label h) PgBouncer single-thread CPU ceiling
